Every now and again, if a pet cat is adjacent to a tree, it should run
straight up there and get stuck.

"The kitten mews helplessly from the top of the tree"

This ought to be quite rare, the odds should be similar to a pet
getting stuck in a pit that it has already identified. Obviosuly,
leashed cats would be immune to tree-trapping. A cat in a tree has a
chance of shaking the odd bit of fruit loose.

I can think of several ways to get cats down from trees:

1) Wait. The cat isn't actually stuck. It just wants to see what *you*
are going to do about the situation. After 50-200 turns it will get
bored and come down.
2) Put a tripe ration on the floor near the tree to tempt the cat down.
3) Magic whistle (or tin opener, if you're patched that way.)
4) If you happen to be levitating/ flying, you can simply (u)ntrap the
cat.
5) Also, if you are polymorphed into a suitably tall creature (eg
giant, mumak) you can use (u)ntrap.
6) Wand of teleport at the cat
7) Wand of polymorph at the cat ("The cat turns into a large kobold!
The large kobold falls out of the tree! The large kobold is killed! You
feel guilty about losing your pet this way.")
8) Kick the tree and try to shake the cat loose. Note that as well as
all inducing all the usual tree-kicking effects, you might hurt your
cat this way ("The cat fails to land on its feet!") or even yourself
("The terrified cat lands on your head!")

Of course this differentiates cats and dogs a little, so for balance
you might want to introduce some kind of tree-sniffing code for dogs
(Every single time they pass a tree they have to stop for a few turns
and have a good sniff. You can pull them away with a leash, but it will
reduce tameness.)



